          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observes, from their garden, an unknown object composed of three glowing orbs arranged in a triangle. The three orbs increase their light intensity before disappearing as if in a strong acceleration. The observation of orange orbs quickly crossing the sky strongly resembles Thai lanterns, likely released nearby after a private party. The movement is observed from west to north, which is consistent with a light southwest wind reported in Caen: Weather. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\", a probable observation of a Thai lantern.",
